        ":question/id": "98a4bd56-0285-5f4b-b31e-2a51803f2189",
        ":question/problem": "$\\int 6^{\\frac{x}{5}}\\,\\text{d}x=$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "If we let $u=\\frac{x}{5},$ then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{5}\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad 5\\,\\text{d}u=\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nThen, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 6^{\\frac{x}{5}}\\,\\text{d}x&=\\int 6^{u}\\cdot 5\\,\\text{d}u \\\\ &=5\\int 6^{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\ &=5\\frac{6^{u}}{\\ln 6}+C \\\\ &=\\frac{5 \\cdot 6^{\\frac{x}{5}}}{\\ln{\\left(6 \\right)}}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"
      },
      "role": "independently authored inventory",
